   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize Hands Across Long Island, Inc. to retroactively apply for a real property tax exemption for certain property in the census-designated place of Ronkonkoma, town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk",
    "basePrintNo": "S4900",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4900-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4900\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize Hands Across Long Island, Inc. to retroactively apply for a\nreal property tax exemption for certain property in the\ncensus-designated place of Ronkonkoma, town of\nBrookhaven, county of Suffolk\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo authorize Hands Across Long Island, Inc. to file for a property tax\nexemption for property owned within the Town of Brookhaven.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would authorize the assessor of the Town of Brookhaven to\naccept from Hands Across Long Island an application or renewal\napplication for exemption from real property taxes as if made\npursuant to 420-a of the Real Property Tax Law. If satisfied that\nHands Across Long Island, Inc. would otherwise have been entitled to\nsuch exemption, the assessor is authorized to grant the same, and\ncancel all remaining unpaid, taxes, interest, related fines and\npenalties.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nHands Across Long Island, Inc. has purchased a piece of real property\nlocated in the Town of Brookhaven for the purpose of providing mental\nhealth services to the community. It is intended by this bill to undo\nthe hardships that will be suffered if the organization is required\nto pay property taxes.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
